  greetings:
  - 'The third guideline is keep your eyes peeled for any links or attachments that
    seem suspicious. This one is harder to spot, as sometimes they can be legitimate
    looking, but generally unless it comes from a trusted source(remember: check
    impersonators!)all emails with links should be disregarded. Examples can include:
    a pdf for no good reason, links to seemingly random websites, or files that need
    to be opened to view the further contents of some email.'
